    "html": "<p>A voltmeter reads <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0\\text{ V}\"></span> when connected across the terminals of a battery in an open circuit. When the battery is connected to a lamp, the voltmeter reading falls to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.6\\text{ V}\"></span> and the current measured in the circuit is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\\text{ A}\"></span>. What is the battery’s internal resistance?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.40\\text{ }\\Omega\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.0\\text{ }\\Omega\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\\text{ }\\Omega\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.5\\text{ }\\Omega\"></span></p></li></ol>"
